# HOSSPI HMS App Write-Up

HOSSPI HMS is the HOSSPI Hospital Management System, where each module must own a focused, self-contained responsibility.

## Core Modules

- Platform: app shell, auth/session, general/tenant/facility settings, users/roles/permissions, subscriptions.
- Spaces and registry: rooms/wards/beds, patient registry.
- Patient care: OPD, triage, clinical, nursing, IPD, ICU, theater, discharge, emergency/ambulance.
- Diagnostics and meds: laboratory, radiology, physiotherapy, pharmacy.
- Finance: billing/cashier, insurance/claims.
- Support: HR, biomedical, operations, housekeeping, mortuary, notifications.
- Cross-cutting: reports/audit, integrations, demo seed, dental.

## Module Boundaries

- Tenant and facility settings own structure; other modules must consume it.
- Access modules own account access; other modules must request allowed actions only.
- Patient-care modules must keep workflows focused and self-contained.
- Reports and audit must read from modules, not replace them.
- Dental must stay within outpatient and emergency dental care.

## Patient Flow Documents

You must use `flows/` when changing workflow behavior:

- `opd-flow.mdc`, `ipd-flow.mdc`, `emergency-flow.mdc`, `icu-flow.mdc`, `theater-flow.mdc`.
- `nursing-flow.mdc`, `lab-flow.mdc`, `radiology-flow.mdc`, `pharmacy-flow.mdc`, `discharge-flow.mdc`.

## Demo Seeds

- Demo data must be clearly marked, safe to reset, and must not be required in production.
